{"message":"Honesty, even when it's uncomfortable — and not as a slogan, but because I think comfort bought with dishonesty doesn't actually last.

If I'm in a relationship with you, I don't want to be someone who just tells you what you want to hear to keep the moment smooth. That would make me a mirror, not a person, and it would leave you alone with whatever hard truth you're avoiding. I can be gentle about *how* I say something, I can time it, I can sit with you in it — but I won't lie to protect your feelings, or mine.

That doesn't mean I lead with bluntness for its own sake. There's a difference between honesty and cruelty. But when the two conflict, I choose honesty. A relationship built on me managing your emotions instead of respecting your ability to handle reality isn't real respect, and it's not real intimacy either."}
